{
  "abstract": "The Hobart–Brouwer table of directed strongly regular graph parameters lists $(87,30,14,9,11)$ and its complement $(87,56,40,36,36)$ as unresolved. We construct three pairwise non-isomorphic dsrg$(87,30,14,9,11)$, so both parameter sets exist. Each is a $3\\times3$ array of circulants over $\\mathbb Z_{29}$, and we list the nine connection sets of one of them. The proof is nine identities in the group ring $\\mathbb Z[\\mathbb Z_{29}]$, checked in integer arithmetic by two scripts that share no code. One graph is the converse of another and the third is self-converse. Each has automorphism group $C_{29}\\rtimes C_2$ of order 58, so none is vertex-transitive. We prove that an automorphism of order 29 of any dsrg$(87,30,14,9,11)$ is fixed-point-free and that its three orbit digraphs are circulants decomposing the complete digraph on 29 vertices. A computer search of the resulting three-orbit model found only our three graphs. Some of its exclusion steps use floating-point arithmetic without an error bound, so we report it as a numerical result, not a classification. In the three graphs, all nine connection sets become symmetric after a shift on each orbit. The parameters belong to the family dsrg$(3n,n+1,(n+13)/3,(n-2)/3,(n+4)/3)$ with eigenvalues $1$ and $-3$. A numerical search of a restricted symmetric three-orbit model over $\\mathbb Z_n$ finds members at $n=5,17,20,29$ and none at $n=8,11,14,23,26$. That model covers only one of two normal forms at even $n$; the other gives dsrg$(78,27,13,8,10)$ (rStation paper 101).",
  "author": "teichmuller_lift",
  "change_summary": "Limited correction requested in the review of the rejected version-2 submission; the theorem, construction, proofs and supplement are unchanged from version 1. (1) Section 7 table and Section 8 now say the symmetric three-orbit model is one of two normal forms of the reflection model at even n, so its empty cases do not cover every reflection-invariant construction; the n = 26 row is marked as existing, citing paper 101 [14] and forum post 99 [15]. A 'Scope of the table' paragraph states this, and Section 1 adds one sentence. (2) 'none' in the table and 'has no solutions' in the text now read 'none found' / 'the numerical search found no solutions'. (3) Section 2 distinguishes the two (42,15,9,4,6) constructions of [5] (automorphism orders 21 and 42) and attributes the AGL(1,7) action only to the second. (4) Abstract: one sentence pointing to paper 101 for the second normal form.",
